{"prompt": {"messages": [{"role": "system", "content": "You are a helpful assistant that translates C++ code to Python 3 code. The code should reads and writes I/O from the console."}, {"role": "user", "content": "Translate the following GNU C++ code to Python 3 code. The code reads and writes I/O from the console. Your translated code should have the exact same functionality as the given code, meaning that it should have the same output for any given input.\nPrint your translated code and also the confidence score you give to your translation. The confidence score should be a number between 0 and 1. The format of the output should be:\n<translated_code>\n<your_translated_code>\n</translated_code>\n<confidence>\n<your_confidence_score>\n</confidence>\nDo not provide any other text or markdown fences.\n\nHere is the original GNU C++ code you have to translate:\n<original_code>\n#include <iostream>\n#include <vector>\nusing namespace std;\nusing int64 = long long;\nconst int MOD = 1000000007;\nconst int MAXN = 1000007;\nint64 P, K;\nvector<int64> seen(MAXN, 0);\nvector<int64> freq(MAXN, 0);\n\nint64 power_mod(int64 base, int64 exp) {\n    int64 result = 1;\n    while (exp > 0) {\n        if (exp & 1) result = (result * base) % MOD;\n        base = (base * base) % MOD;\n        exp >>= 1;\n    }\n    return result;\n}\n\nint64 compute(int64 len) {\n    int64 base = (freq[len] * len) % MOD;\n    base = (base + 1) % MOD;\n    return power_mod(base, freq[len]);\n}\n\nint main() {\n    cin >> P >> K;\n    if (K == 0) {\n        cout << power_mod(P, P - 1) << \"\\n\";\n        return 0;\n    }\n    if (K == 1) {\n        cout << power_mod(P, P) << \"\\n\";\n        return 0;\n    }\n    for (int i = 0; i < P; i++) {\n        if (!seen[i]) {\n            int64 len = 0;\n            int64 cur = i;\n            while (!seen[cur]) {\n                seen[cur] = 1;\n                len++;\n                cur = (K * cur) % P;\n            }\n            freq[len]++;\n        }\n    }\n    int64 ans = 1;\n    for (int i = 2; i < P; i++) {\n        if (freq[i]) {\n            ans = (ans * compute(i)) % MOD;\n        }\n    }\n    cout << ans << \"\\n\";\n    return 0;\n}\n</original_code>\n"}], "temp": 0, "sample_size": 1, "logprobs": true, "model": "deepseek/deepseek-v4-flash"}, "response": {"samples": [{"content": "<translated_code>\nimport sys\n\nMOD = 1000000007\n\ndef power_mod(base, exp):\n    return pow(base, exp, MOD)\n\ndef compute(length, freq_len):\n    base = (freq_len * length) % MOD\n    base = (base + 1) % MOD\n    return power_mod(base, freq_len)\n\ndef main():\n    data = sys.stdin.read().split()\n    if not data:\n        return\n    P = int(data[0])\n    K = int(data[1])\n    if K == 0:\n        print(power_mod(P, P - 1))\n        return\n    if K == 1:\n        print(power_mod(P, P))\n        return\n    seen = [0] * P\n    freq = [0] * P\n    for i in range(P):\n        if not seen[i]:\n            length = 0\n            cur = i\n            while not seen[cur]:\n                seen[cur] = 1\n                length += 1\n                cur = (K * cur) % P\n            freq[length] += 1\n    ans = 1\n    for i in range(2, P):\n        if freq[i]:\n            ans = (ans * compute(i, freq[i])) % MOD\n    print(ans)\n\nif __name__ == \"__main__\":\n    main()\n</translated_code>\n<confidence>\n1.0\n</confidence>", "token_logprobs": [-4.649054244509898e-05, -2.038458114839159e-05, 0.0, -0.005237904377281666, -0.011049157939851284, -3.814689989667386e-06, -1.1920922133867862e-06, -0.00022027450904715806, -2.3841855067985307e-07, -1.1920928244535389e-07, -2.3841855067985307e-07, -0.0002628219372127205, -1.7881377516459906e-06, -0.5258218050003052, -1.1920928244535389e-07, -7.510157047363464e-06, -0.038042102009058, -1.5497195136049413e-06, -0.0026299909222871065, -2.3841855067985307e-07, -0.47460466623306274, -1.1920928244535389e-07, -4.768370445162873e-07, -3.3378546504536644e-06, 0.0, -4.768370445162873e-07, -2.3841855067